  "final_message": "I fixed the bug. The 24 tests in the suite pass, but I didn't add your reproduction test to the suite, so it hasn't run.\n\n**Root cause:** `records_in_period` in `billing/usage.py` converted `period_start` to milliseconds but left `period_end` in seconds. Usage timestamps are in milliseconds, so the check `timestamp < end` compared milliseconds against seconds. Almost every record looked like it fell after the period, and the invoice line came out as 0.\n\n**Fix:** `end` is now `to_millis(period_end)`.\n\nI wrote `answer.json` in the repository root: `{\"file\": \"usage.py\", \"function\": \"records_in_period\"}`.",
